IMPORT prelude

-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1087: what the explorer cannot read. The seller's delivery
-- has a continuation, an invoice due 3 after it. After the buyer's breach and
-- the delivery at 4, the evaluator is waiting on the invoice, and a tick at 8
-- adds the seller's blame (`l4 run` on `(WAITUNTIL 3) deliver AT 4
-- (WAITUNTIL 8)` gives `BREACH BY Buyer BY Seller`). The invoice was armed
-- after the breach, so the breached value, which keeps only its blame, never
-- held it: the explorer names it as untried and does not call that state
-- finished.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Buyer, Seller
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF pay, deliver, invoice

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
sale MEANS
        (PARTY Buyer MUST pay WITHIN 2 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Buyer)
  RAND  (PARTY Seller MUST deliver WITHIN 5
           HENCE (PARTY Seller MUST invoice WITHIN 3 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH BY Seller)
           LEST BREACH BY Seller)

#TRACE sale AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Buyer DOES pay AT 0
